# SHEscale — Project Plan

*A unified funding, mentorship, and networking ecosystem for female entrepreneurs*

---

## 1. What We Are Building

**SHEscale** is a single, unified web workspace — not three disconnected apps — that takes a woman entrepreneur through the entire lifecycle of building a business:

1. **Getting capital** (Funding Hub) — finding the right government scheme, understanding the paperwork, submitting clean applications, and planning finances.
2. **Getting guidance** (Mentorship Hub) — practicing pitches, getting 24/7 AI coaching, and eventually earning access to real human mentors.
3. **Getting community** (Networking Hub) — finding a co-founder, finding nearby non-competing businesses to partner with, and getting small emergency capital from other women in the network while bank loans are still processing.

All three live inside one dashboard with a shared identity/profile layer, so the user never has to re-enter her business context three times.

---

## 2. Why We Are Building It

**The core problem:** Government schemes like Mudra Loan and Stand-Up India exist specifically to fund women entrepreneurs — but almost no one uses them effectively because of three compounding failures:

| Failure | Real-world effect |
|---|---|
| **Discovery failure** | Women don't know which of the 20+ overlapping schemes they actually qualify for. |
| **Comprehension failure** | Scheme details live in 30–40 page government PDFs full of legal/financial jargon, so even eligible women give up or apply incorrectly. |
| **Confidence failure** | Even with the money identified, most first-time founders have never faced a bank loan officer or VC and don't know how to defend their numbers — so they walk in underprepared and get rejected. |
| **Isolation failure** | Solo founders have no technical co-founder, no peer network, and no bridge capital while formal loans are stuck in processing for weeks. |

SHEscale exists to collapse all four failures into one guided, AI-assisted journey — turning a scattered, intimidating bureaucratic process into something as simple as a conversation.

---

## 3. Who It Is For

| Persona | Situation | What SHEscale gives her |
|---|---|---|
| **The First-Time Founder** | Has a business idea (e.g. an organic boutique) but has never dealt with government paperwork or banks. | Plain-language scheme matching + PDF-Whisperer + document scanner so she doesn't get rejected on a technicality. |
| **The Solo Technical/Business Builder** | Has half the skillset (e.g. a BCA student who can code, or a marketer with no product person). | Skill-based swipe-matching to find a complementary co-founder. |
| **The Pitch-Anxious Applicant** | Has a solid plan but freezes up or under-prepares in front of a real bank/VC. | The AI Mock Interviewer + Readiness Score Matrix, so the *first* hard conversation happens with an AI, not the real loan officer. |
| **The Cash-Gap Founder** | Loan is approved in principle but stuck in bank processing for 3–6 weeks with rent/inventory due now. | The Micro-Grant Community Ledger for small bridge capital from other women in the network. |
| **The Scaling Founder** | Business is running, and now she's ready for real strategic help, not basic Q&A. | Unlocked access to vetted human mentors, arriving with a pre-formatted AI-vetted brief so the call is high-value from minute one. |

---

## 4. How We Are Building It

**Architecture approach:** A single React-based dashboard, one core Node.js/Express backend, one shared MongoDB data layer (see the earlier schema-design prompt), with the Gemini API doing the heavy semantic/document/voice lifting across all three pillars rather than three separate AI stacks.

**Core technical building blocks:**
- **Semantic scheme matching** — natural language business description → Gemini extracts structured parameters → matched against a scheme eligibility ruleset.
- **Document intelligence** — PDF parsing + structural prompting to turn dense legal text into scannable eligibility cards, financial terms, and red-flag alerts.
- **Computer-vision-lite document QA** — canvas-based blur/crop detection on uploads before they ever reach a human reviewer.
- **Conversational financial modeling** — natural language unit economics → auto-generated 3-year P&L and break-even visualizations.
- **Voice AI simulation** — Gemini Live API over WebRTC for real-time mock bank/VC interviews, with a post-session scored readiness matrix.
- **Matching algorithms** — skill-vector and location-tier matching for co-founders and nearby non-competing businesses.
- **Community ledger** — a transactional micro-funding feed with live progress bars.

**Design principle throughout:** every complex, intimidating process (a 40-page PDF, a bank interview, a financial model) gets converted into something visual, conversational, and immediate — never a form the user has to fill out cold.

---

## 5. 🆕 New Feature: Live Government Scheme Intelligence Panel

**What it does:**
Beyond just matching a user to a scheme she already asked about, SHEscale actively pulls and displays the **exact live process, eligibility guidelines, required documents, and newly launched schemes** directly from official government scheme portals (e.g. Jan Samarth, Startup India, Stand-Up India, Mudra Yojana, state MSME portals) — presented through the same clean, scannable UI as the PDF Doc-Whisperer, instead of sending the user away to read a government website.

**Why it matters:**
Government portals change scheme terms, launch new schemes, or update interest rates and deadlines with little notice — and most existing tools (including basic scheme matchers) go stale. This feature keeps SHEscale as a *living*, always-current source of truth, not a one-time database snapshot, so users never miss a newly launched scheme they'd qualify for.

**How it works:**
1. A backend scheduled job periodically fetches/refreshes structured data from official government scheme sources (name, eligibility, required documents, interest rate, deadlines, application steps).
2. Each refreshed scheme is passed through the same Gemini structural-extraction pipeline used in the PDF Doc-Whisperer, so it lands in the same clean visual format: **Green Eligibility Cards**, **Financial Pills**, and **Alert Boxes** for new rules or deadline changes.
3. A **"What's New"** ribbon/section on the Funding Hub dashboard surfaces newly added or recently updated schemes first, so returning users immediately see what changed since their last visit.
4. Each scheme card includes a **live step-by-step application guideline** (the real government process, not a paraphrase) rendered as the same Stepper UI already used for the user's own document tracker — so she can preview the *entire* real-world process before she even starts.
5. This feed directly powers the Conversational Scheme Matcher (Feature 1.1) — matching is always run against the current live scheme set, not a fixed list, so the AI never recommends an outdated or discontinued scheme.

**UI/UX treatment (kept consistent with the platform's existing visual language):**
- Same card-based, color-coded system as the PDF Doc-Whisperer (green = eligible, red = alert/deadline, blue pill = financial terms) so this feels like a native part of the Funding Hub, not a bolted-on news feed.
- A subtle "last synced" timestamp per scheme card builds trust that the data is current.
- New/updated schemes get a small non-intrusive badge (not a disruptive popup) — respecting the calm, guided tone of the rest of the dashboard.
- Filter/sort controls (by state, business type, loan size) so the live feed doesn't overwhelm a first-time visitor.

---

## 6. Suggested Phased Rollout

| Phase | Focus |
|---|---|
| **Phase 1 — MVP** | Auth/Profile, Conversational Scheme Matcher, PDF Doc-Whisperer, basic Document Tracker |
| **Phase 2** | Live Government Scheme Intelligence Panel, BizCalculus Financial Planner |
| **Phase 3** | AI Twin Mentor, AI Mock Interviewer + Readiness Score |
| **Phase 4** | Human Mentor Booking, Co-founder Swipe-Matching |
| **Phase 5** | Hyper-Local Ecosystem Blueprint, Micro-Grant Community Ledger |

This sequencing front-loads the features that solve the most urgent failure (discovery + comprehension of funding) before layering in mentorship and community, which matter more once a founder already has capital clarity.